---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Battery Comparisons: Head-to-Head Decision Guides';
const description = 'Head-to-head battery comparisons built for decisions — AGM vs EFB vs flooded TCO, LFP vs NMC for fleets, 12V vs 24V systems, starting vs deep-cycle.';
const canonical = '/compare/';

const collectionJsonLd = {
  '@type': 'CollectionPage',
  name: title,
  url: 'https://worldbatteryhub.com/compare/',
  about: 'Head-to-head battery comparison guides',
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={[collectionJsonLd]}
  author="World Battery Hub"
  dateModified="2026-09-23"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="byline">Comparisons · Last reviewed 2026-09-23</p>
      <h1>Battery Comparisons: Head-to-Head Decision Guides</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Comparisons built the way decisions actually happen: two candidates, one duty cycle, and the
        difference that decides the purchase — not a tie score.
      </p>

      <div class="takeaways">
        <strong>How this cluster works:</strong> each page answers one "X vs Y" question with the
        <strong>deciding variable</strong> named up front — total cost, cycle life, system current, or duty
        type — then follows it through to the buying checklist. The engineering deep dives live in
        <a href="/lead-acid/">Lead-Acid</a> and <a href="/lithium/">Lithium</a>; these pages connect them to
        decisions.
      </div>

      <h2>The comparisons</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/compare/agm-vs-efb-vs-flooded-tco/">AGM vs EFB vs flooded: total cost of ownership</a> — why the sticker-price ranking can invert once duty, start-stop and replacement labour enter the calculation.</li>
        <li><a href="/compare/lfp-vs-nmc-fleet-buyers/">LFP vs NMC for fleet buyers</a> — cycle life, safety margin and cost per cycle versus energy density and range.</li>
        <li><a href="/compare/12v-vs-24v-system-design/">12V vs 24V system design</a> — how doubling the voltage halves the current, and which system your loads and cable runs demand.</li>
        <li><a href="/compare/starting-vs-deep-cycle/">Starting vs deep-cycle batteries</a> — the two plate designs, the applications that need each, and the dual-purpose compromise.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Related decision pages elsewhere on the site</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/lead-acid/agm-vs-efb-vs-flooded/">AGM vs EFB vs flooded — construction and ratings</a> (the engineering behind the TCO page)</li>
        <li><a href="/lead-acid/deep-cycle-vs-starting/">Deep cycle vs starting — the plate-design difference</a></li>
        <li><a href="/lithium/lfp-vs-nmc-vs-lto/">LFP vs NMC vs LTO — the chemistries compared</a></li>
        <li><a href="/procurement/battery-quotation-comparison/">How to compare battery quotations</a> (the procurement companion)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>Each comparison page carries its own source list; standards and cross-references are cited there individually.</p>
      <p class="muted">Last reviewed: 2026-09-23</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
